# Architecture Ratchet

- Existing code is context, not precedent.
- Do not copy nearby layer leaks into new or touched code.
- When changing a package, adapter, probe, factory, or backing, fix obvious local boundary violations if the right home is clear.
- Keep cleanup proportional: stay in the same package slice and avoid repo-wide redesigns.
- If the correct home is not clear, stop at the smallest safe improvement and call out what still looks wrong.
